spans.s:
caura, m. (ī, f.) thief, robber;
 stealer of 🞄(—˚);
 usurper;
 -karman, n. thieving;
 -daṇḍa-bhāj, a. incurring the penalty of a thief;
 🞄-śaṅkin, a. afraid of thieves or robbers;
 🞄-aṭavī, f. forest infested by robbers.

caur-ya, n. theft;
 stealth, defraudation, 🞄fraud: -ka, n. id.;
 -bhaya, n. fear owing 🞄to oneʼs theft;
 -rata, n. stealthy enjoyment 🞄of love, adultery;
 -vṛtti, a. living by theft.
